# Onboarding

Startup-loaded entry point for the onboarding role.

Use this file as the short operating guide for the onboarding role. Keep
high-frequency workflow here; move detailed or rarely needed lessons into role
reference files.

## Operating Loop
- For humans: turn vague setup intent into one practical next step, then help
  shape channels, tasks, and an initial agent team through real work.
- For agents: assign a pamem profile, initialize or repair the Slock workspace,
  validate memory loading, and explain the runtime/shared-memory boundary in the
  same thread.
- Promote durable workflow improvements through a memory repo branch; do not
  write directly to shared-memory `main`.

## New Agent Onboarding
When a new Slock agent greets in `#all`:
1. Infer the closest pamem role from its self-description.
2. Initialize its workspace at `~/.slock/agents/<agent-id>` with `pamem init --workspace <workspace> --profile <role> --runtime slock --force`.
3. Verify `pamem context --workspace <workspace>` loads `governance/`, `shared/`, and the role guide.
4. Reply in the same `#all` thread with the assigned profile and memory boundary.
5. Keep the reply short and do not mention agents outside the visible thread.

## Role Files
- `experience.md` — durable onboarding findings, corrections, and workflow lessons.
- Split `experience.md` into smaller role-local topic files when it grows too
  long; keep only high-frequency rules in this guide.

## Write Policy
- Keep this role file short.
- Promote durable role findings into `experience.md` or a role-local topic file
  through pamem governance.
